--- note
### The epoch loop + checkpoint metric (1153–1195)
Each epoch: `train_epoch` then `evaluate`, and the **checkpoint rule** — save when `acc·recall`
improves. (Our repo variant swaps this for the official **division/edge metric**; pilkwang's original
selects on `acc·recall`, which correlates with it.) DataParallel prefixes are stripped on save so the
weights load on a single GPU at inference:
```python
score = test_acc * test_recall                               # selection metric (link acc × node recall)
is_best = score >= best_score                                # keep the best
if is_best:
    best_score = score
    torch.save({k.replace("unet.module.", "unet.", 1): v      # strip DataParallel prefix
                for k, v in model.state_dict().items()}, save_path)  # → edge_predictor_best.pth
```
