--- note
### `main()` + CLI (1198–1279) — the flags you actually type
`argparse` exposes every knob covered above. The important ones:
```
--split 0            CV fold                --epochs 50          training length
--lr 1e-4            AdamW learning rate     --batch-size 16      windows per step
--unet-out-channels 32   UNet feature width  --unet-layers 32,64,128   encoder stages
--downsample 1,4,4   Z,Y,X strides (I/O)     --det-loss-weight 1.0     weight of det vs edge loss
--det-neg-weight 1e-2   recall tilt          --window-size 2      frames per window (W)
--pool-kernel-um 5.0    NMS radius (µm)       --data-parallel / --single-gpu   multi-GPU UNet
--unet-weights PATH  warm-start the UNet      --max-iters N        cap iters (smoke run)
```
`main()` parses these, resolves `data_dir`/`splits`, and calls `train(...)`. Run it exactly as the
docstring shows: `uv run scripts/train_unet_transformer.py --split 0 --epochs 50`. **This completes
the full line-by-line walkthrough of the main trainer** — from imports (tr01) through the CLI (tr06).

